/*! \page e3_system_design E3 and dApp Runtime System Design

Git Markdown companion: \c docs/dapp/e3_system_design.md (normative prose).

\section e3_design_goals Goals

Fault-contained trusted packages near the modem; hard real-time isolation of
management, staging and telemetry from slot workers; backend-neutral C ABI;
composable sensing and control through host caches; operable lifecycle with
generations, jobs, metrics and incidents; observation for out-of-process
dApps without touching the radio path.

\section e3_design_components Components

\ref ocudu::app_services::dapp_service owns the catalog, verifier,
instance manager and native hook registry, and the embedded E3 agent:
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::embedded_agent (jobs),
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::management_service (request validation and dispatch),
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::portable_data_store (bounded publication queues),
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::telemetry_publisher (upper-PHY diagnostics and gNB JSON
into the store), \ref ocudu::dapp::e3::local_management_server,
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::e3ap_sctp_server and
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::e3dp_sctp_server (carriers). The SCTP carriers share
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::sctp_association_server, a single-threaded association
core with message-boundary framing, bounded outbound queues, peer filtering and
idle close.

\section e3_design_timing Timing classes

Class A resident inline L1 (enqueue-bound, in process), Class B deadline-bound
decisions (~100 µs boundary, in-process authority), Class C open-loop analytics
(native or supervised process). Telemetry and E3 are Class-C-adjacent
observation: producers pay one bounded copy and never wait.

\section e3_design_data Data paths

Native CPU/CUDA routes, process SHM/CUDA-IPC routes, portable E3 host
snapshots (pull over the management socket or push over E3AP), and telemetry
streams (PUSCH symbols/CRC, SRS/DM-RS estimates, gNB JSON) gated by
\c has_active before capture. Single spectrum result authority; observers only
consume.

\section e3_design_placement Agent placement

Management executors only; one non-real-time thread per SCTP carrier; never
invoked from slot indication or PUSCH worker threads. Store queues are
preallocated per subscription; overload drops whole objects according to the
subscription's drop policy and is counted.

\section e3_design_trust Trust posture

Admitted packages are trusted native code; signing binds what was admitted.
Supervised Class C adds fault containment. SCTP endpoints bind loopback by
default; there is no TLS in v1. Management over E3AP carries full management
authority.

\section e3_design_versioning Versioning

Manifest schema v1, management ASN.1 v1, E3AP and telemetry ASN.1 v1, Class-C
FlatBuffers v1, data-profile FlatBuffers v1, public C ABI v1. Extension
additions live behind \c ... markers.

\section e3_design_related Related

\ref e3_wire, \ref e3_management, \ref dapp_observability.
*/
